\ Expansion erases the call to an `inline` word, so nothing pushes that word's frame. The chain
\ has to name it anyway, out of the side table the expansion pass records.
\
\ Without the marker this is error_frames_chain_direct.1z, whose golden carries the same three
\ rows. With it, `inner` has no call left at run time and its row is synthesized instead.
\
\ No flags: one golden binds the interpreted and eager suites, which is the pin that the
\ synthesized row reads the same whether the caller ran interpreted or compiled.

inner: ( s v -- n ) const inline [ stream-write 0 + ] ;
outer: ( s v -- n ) [ inner 0 + ] ;

stdout 42 outer .
